[?2004l[?2004h> +over label rows ordered by ``label_available_at``.  For each prediction we merge the most recent
[?2004l[?2004h> +cumulative statistics that are strictly before the prediction's ``as_of`` timestamp, then apply the
[?2004l[?2004h> +smoothed formula:
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +```
[?2004l[?2004h> +te = (s + m * p) / (n + m)
[?2004l[?2004h> +```
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +where ``p`` is the overall prior mean computed from the same set of *available* label rows (i.e.
[?2004l[?2004h> +those with ``label_available_at < t``).  If no label rows are available for a given ``t`` we fall back
[?2004l[?2004h> +to the constant ``DEFAULT_PRIOR``.
[?2004l[?2004h> +"""
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +import pandas as pd
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +PRIOR_WEIGHT = 20
[?2004l[?2004h> +DEFAULT_PRIOR = 0.05
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +def district_encoding(points, labels, customers, m=PRIOR_WEIGHT):
[?2004l[?2004h> +    """Return the smoothed churn rate per postcode district respecting label availability.
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +    Parameters
[?2004l[?2004h> +    ----------
[?2004l[?2004h> +    points : DataFrame
[?2004l[?2004h> +        Scoring points with ``customer_id`` and ``as_of``.
[?2004l[?2004h> +    labels : DataFrame
[?2004l[?2004h> +        Label rows containing ``customer_id``, ``churned_30d`` and ``label_available_at``.
[?2004l[?2004h> +    customers : DataFrame
[?2004l[?2004h> +        Customer master with ``customer_id`` and ``postcode_district``.
[?2004l[?2004h> +    m : int, optional
[?2004l[?2004h> +        Prior weight (default 20).
[?2004l[?2004h> +    """
[?2004l[?2004h> +    # Map customers to districts
[?2004l[?2004h> +    district_map = customers.set_index("customer_id")["postcode_district"]
[?2004l[?2004h> +    points = points.copy()
[?2004l[?2004h> +    points["district"] = points["customer_id"].map(district_map)
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +    # Prepare labels with district information
[?2004l[?2004h> +    lbl = labels.copy()
[?2004l[?2004h> +    lbl["district"] = lbl["customer_id"].map(district_map)
[?2004l[?2004h> +    # Drop rows where district could not be resolved (should be rare)
